Osiris IDE — sample tracked patch
=================================

This is a demonstration patch showing how Osiris carries downstream changes on
top of the pinned VSCodium tag. `scripts/apply-branding.mjs` runs `git apply
--3way` for every `patches/*.patch`; a patch that no longer applies is skipped
with a warning (so an upstream bump never hard-fails the branding step — you
re-roll the patch instead).

Replace the body below with a real unified diff generated against the upstream
checkout, e.g.:

    cd apps/osiris-desktop/.build/vscodium
    # ...make your change...
    git diff > ../../patches/0002-my-change.patch

--- a/src/vs/workbench/browser/parts/titlebar/titlebarPart.ts
+++ b/src/vs/workbench/browser/parts/titlebar/titlebarPart.ts
@@ -1,3 +1,4 @@
+// Osiris IDE downstream marker — replace this placeholder patch with a real diff.
